  "id": "sturgeweber-syndrome",
  "term": "Sturge–Weber syndrome",
  "definition": "Sturge–Weber syndrome is a congenital condition that is not inherited and involves abnormal blood vessels and neurological changes. It is marked by a facial port-wine stain and abnormal capillaries in the brain coverings and eye, and it can be associated with epilepsy, cognitive impairment, glaucoma, and vision problems.",
